From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:59:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Haswell NRI: Fix per-bit sense amp offset packing

When packing the per-bit read Vref offsets into RX_OFFSET_VDQ, `<<`
binds tighter than `&`, so `vref & 0xf << (4 * bit)` masks vref with
0xf0, 0xf00 and so on. Since vref is at most 15, only bit 0 keeps its
trained value; bits 1 to 7 of every byte lane end up with code 0, the
most negative offset (8 is neutral), instead of the trained one. The
"BitSAmp" log line prints the correct values, which hides the issue.
Nothing rewrites the register later and it is saved for fast boot and
S3 resume, so this costs read voltage margin on every boot.

Shift the clamped value into place and OR it into the register value.
Bump the register frame revision so that cached training data with the
broken offsets is discarded and trained again.

Fixes: commit 5d291de6011a ("haswell NRI: Do sense amplifier offset training")

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541 with native raminit. Checked on the host
that the packed value for per-bit codes 8,7,9,8,6,8,a,7 is 0x7a868978
(was 0x00000008). Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c  | 5 ++++-
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_sense_amp_offset.c    | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
index 5be68808d..6e199d344 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
@@ -14,8 +14,11 @@ uint32_t reg_frame_rev(void)
 	 * The structures that get saved to flash are contained within
 	 * this translation unit, so changes outside this file shouldn't
 	 * require invalidating the cache.
+	 *
+	 * Exception: revision 2 discards data saved with broken per-bit
+	 * sense amplifier offsets, so that they get trained again.
 	 */
-	return 1;
+	return 2;
 }
 
 struct register_save {
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_sense_amp_offset.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_sense_amp_offset.c
index 6989dd631..938ae70a3 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_sense_amp_offset.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_sense_amp_offset.c
@@ -299,7 +299,7 @@ static void train_samp_offset(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 					vref = 0;
 
 				ctrl->rxdqvrefpb[channel][0][byte][bit].center = vref;
-				rx_offset_vdq += vref & 0xf << (4 * bit);
+				rx_offset_vdq |= (uint32_t)vref << (4 * bit);
 				printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "%x", vref);
 			}
 			mchbar_write32(RX_OFFSET_VDQ(channel, byte), rx_offset_vdq);
